From e7f517469707b43940f23625edd359d961224f9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 13:09:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): a park never waits on something already true:
 skip done producers, refuse a passing wake_check [daveey]

MacBook card t_01a18c12b9e15db0, run by a hub worker, parked twice (continuations 6 and 7, 10-30) with
awaiting={kind:'card', ref:'t_01a1848506cae619', inferred:true} and the auto probe `hermes kanban wait-check
task t_01a1848506cae619`. That card completed two hours earlier and was named only as background (the real
wait was main CI), so each probe exited 0 at once and the card woke in 7-16 s.

- _live_card_ref skips a done card: a finished card produces nothing later. With no other live card named,
  inference falls through to the external/clock classification unchanged.
- A declared awaiting={kind:'card'} on a done card is refused producer_done (local: _check_card; another
  gateway: confirm_remote on a `done` status word). Remote review/blocked rc-0 statuses stay parkable: a
  tracker's re-park probe reads a handled status as "not yet" (implicit --from), refusing them would strand it.
  Deferred placement settles (completes) a forwarded card whose remote run finished between read and confirm.
- The park-time dry run of an explicit wake_check (kanban_schedule, kanban_continue, kanban_block, the CLI)
  refuses exit 0 with wake_check_already_true and the probe's output tail; with blocker_id it says the wall is
  gone and points to clear_blocker=true. Exit 1, a timeout or anything else is unchanged. The dry run carries
  the dispatcher's probe marker so wait-check's implicit --from matches the first real probe.

Card t_01a18cd86aa64a14. Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_park_done_producer.py (8 RED on 418c075690f,
the 2 park controls pass both ways); test_kanban_cli's block test used `test -f /tmp/x`, which exists on the hub.
